  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "0J62etBOS4Yo6dfufsiyfROfqxJL56EsUKWgMWuLWhv6Fm8slUnMeIriAzFVgUiwsIbXVSD09ENJ/bqVkkjsiQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 245614,
  "published": "2026-08-05T20:57:33.617Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.17: removing a role assignment no longer runs the create validator -- read UPGRADE.md section 30. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: DeleteUserRoleAssignmentAsync, DeleteUserRoleAssignmentIfExistsAsync and the pre-check of UpdateUserRoleAssignmentAsync used to re-validate the already-persisted row through the helper that validates a NEW assignment, which asks whether the role exists, is not a system role, and belongs to the target user's tenant. Deleting a role does not delete the assignment rows pointing at it (no foreign key on RoleId, only on UserId), so afterwards a TenantAdmin got MyIdentityErrorCodes.RoleNotFound when removing the leftover row while a SystemAdmin removed it fine. The pre-check now asks only whether the row belongs to the caller's tenant. Nothing was loosened: removing a grant is de-escalation, the surviving check still confines the target user to the caller's tenant, AddUserRoleAssignmentAsync is unchanged, and UpdateUserRoleAssignmentAsync still fully validates the incoming values. Repairing a stale row by pointing it at a valid role is now possible. Added: MyIdentity:FineGrainedPermissions:OnPermissionNarrowing binds from appsettings (code still wins), with a misspelled or out-of-range value failing in the curated startup report instead of as a raw binder exception. That adds OnPermissionNarrowing() to IMyIdentityConfigurationService -- source- AND binary-breaking for a hand-rolled implementation of that interface: an already-compiled implementation fails at type load with TypeLoadException until recompiled. API may still change before stable.",
